from h import *
A = dict(id="A", levels=L1, kind="Web page", source="Fennbridge Bikes website", title="Fennbridge Bikes: hire a bike for £1", body=[
 {"p": "Pick up a bike at any of our 20 docking stations and return it to any other station. The first 30 minutes cost just £1. Bikes are available every day from 6 am to 10 pm."},
 {"callout": "I cycle to work now and I save £30 a month on bus fares! - Sam, a Fennbridge Bikes user"},
 {"p": "Download our free app to find your nearest bike. You can also see how many bikes are waiting at each station."}])
B = dict(id="B", levels=L1, kind="Council report", source="Vale of Fenn Council", title="Fennbridge Bikes: six months on", body=[
 {"h": "Introduction"},
 {"p": "Fennbridge Bikes began six months ago with 200 bikes and 20 docking stations. This report looks at how the scheme has been used and suggests ways to improve it. The scheme is run by Vale of Fenn Council and is paid for partly by a grant."},
 {"h": "How many people have used it?"},
 {"p": "Since the launch, there have been over 14,000 hires. Saturday is the busiest day, and the most popular journey is from the railway station to Market Square. Most users are commuters and students, and hires are highest in the summer, when the weather is dry and the evenings are light. The council leader said, \"The scheme has been a huge success.\""},
 {"h": "Costs and savings"},
 {"p": "The first 30 minutes of every hire cost £1, which is cheaper than the bus fare for the same journey. Bike hire also cuts traffic, which helps to keep the air cleaner. Users who cycle to work every day could save up to £30 a month. Running the scheme costs the council about £2,000 a month, which is covered by hire fees and a grant."},
 {"h": "Problems"},
 {"p": "Not everything has gone well. The docking station at the railway station is often full in the evening, so cyclists have to ride to another station to return their bikes. Some bikes have also been damaged, and these must be repaired before they can be used again. Staff visit each docking station every day to move bikes from full stations to empty ones. A small number of users' comments say that there are not enough stations in the east of the town."},
 {"h": "Recommendations"},
 {"p": "The council should add a second docking station near the railway station, buy 50 more bikes and open three new stations in the east of the town. These changes are the best way to improve the scheme."}])
C = dict(id="C", levels=L1, kind="Forum post", source="Fennbridge Talk forum, thread: \"Anyone tried the bikes?\"", title="Re: Anyone tried the bikes?", body=[
 {"p": "Hey everyone! I've been using the bikes for about two months now and honestly I love them."},
 {"p": "I live near the market and I work at the hospital, so it takes me ten minutes to get there instead of half an hour on the bus. I also like that you can go through the park, where cars aren't allowed. Honestly, I haven't used my bus pass since, and it's saving me loads of money too. The app is brilliant too. It shows you exactly how many bikes are free at each station."},
 {"p": "But there are a few problems. Last Friday I got to the station at about 6 pm and the dock was totally full. I had to cycle round for ages to find a free space, and I nearly missed my train! Also, a couple of the bikes I picked up had wonky brakes, which is scary."},
 {"p": "My tips:"},
 {"ul": ["Check the app before you set off, so you know where there are free spaces.", "Test the brakes before you ride away.", "Take the bike back within 30 minutes if you can, because it costs more after that."]},
 {"p": "Has anyone else had trouble finding a space at the station?"}])

